From: BPI-W2 PiKVM <jalen.lin@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] m2m: support single-planar encoders, such as coda

The M2M encoder only spoke the multi-planar API of the Raspberry Pi's
bcm2835-codec. The mainline coda driver, which runs the RTD1296's CODA980
H.264 encoder on the BPI-W2, is single-planar. Pick the API from
VIDIOC_QUERYCAP and use struct v4l2_pix_format and plain buffers for it.

Also:
- Capture hardware that aligns the plane height (1080 to 1088) starts the
  chroma plane after the padding rows. On the single-planar path, give the
  encoder the aligned height and crop back to the real one with
  VIDIOC_S_SELECTION, so the SPS carries frame cropping.
- Treat controls that not every encoder has as optional: coda has GOP_SIZE
  instead of H264_I_PERIOD, no REPEAT_SEQ_HEADER (it puts SPS/PPS before
  every IDR anyway) and, being a CODA960 family member, no H264_MIN_QP.

diff --git a/src/ustreamer/m2m.c b/src/ustreamer/m2m.c
index d0b08ae..3b77245 100644
--- a/src/ustreamer/m2m.c
+++ b/src/ustreamer/m2m.c
